  "description": "RISVUM crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C10 H14 Ce6 N4 O40 2-,5(H4 N1 1+),3(N1 O3 1-),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.710-3.839 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.69-120.07°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6(μ3-O)4(μ3-OH)4(HCOO)10(NO3)4]·(NO3)3(NH4)5(H2O)5. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
